  "sources": [
    "https://help.gnome.org/users/gnome-help/stable/shell-keyboard-shortcuts.html.en",
    "https://help.gnome.org/users/gnome-help/stable/keyboard-shortcuts-set.html.en"
  ],
  "note": "GNOME Shell defaults as shipped by Ubuntu. GNOME's Super key is written Win. Rows GNOME lists as Disabled by default are left out (Decrease/Increase text size, high contrast, on-screen keyboard, hide all normal windows, workspaces 2-4, raise/lower window, maximize horizontally/vertically, toggle fullscreen, window on all workspaces, switch windows, switch windows of an application). Left out because the chord grammar cannot express them: the bare Super key (Activities overview) and the Launchers section, which is bound to hardware keys (Explorer, Calculator, Mail, WWW, Search, Tools); the Print-key screenshot shortcuts (Print, Alt+Print, Shift+Print), because there is no Print Screen key in the grammar; and the Sound and Media rows with no matching media key (pause, stop, eject, launch media player, microphone mute).",
